Amazon Elastic compute cloud (EC2):- 

Service that provides secure, resizable compute capacity in the cloud.
It allow you to provision a server on aws within minutes.
Multiple EC2 instances can be deployed on a single server using virtual machines.
VPCs are used to logically isolate each customers infrastructure. 

Amazon Machine Image (AMI):- 
AMI is an image that provides the information required to launch an EC2 instance.
AMi is an blueprint that contains information such as what OS and what software/packages should be installed on an instance. 
We can use this blueprint(ami) to deploy identical EC2 instances.
There is different AMIs for diff OS for diff services and features.
Think of the AMI as an installer disk used for installing a new server. 
AMIs can be fully customised. add application source code, add dependency, OS , firewall etc.

Instance Types:-
EC2 provides wide selection of instances types optimised to fit different use cases.
It has varying combinations of cpu, memory, storage, and networking capacity. 
Think of instance types of server models to select from. 

1) Gernal purpose:- Provide good balance of compute, memory, and networking resources.
		 Can be used for diverse workloads. 
		 Ideal for app that use resources in equal proportion.

2) Compute Optimized:- Optimized for compute-heavy applications. 
		  Contain high performance cpu. 
		  Ideal for batch processing workloands, media transcoding, machine learning, and gaming servers.

3) Memory Optimized:- Deliver fast performance for memory intensive workloads. suited for database.

4) storage Optimized:- Optimized for workloads that require high sequential read and write access to large data sets on local storage.  
Can deliver tens of thousands of low-letency random operations per sec(IOPS).

5) Accelerated Computing:- Utilized hardware accelerators to perform expensive calculations. 
			Great for graphics processing and data pattern matching. 
